245:<h2 id="stop">Stopping the link (runbook, written in E-2)</h2>
247:  <li><strong>Immediately</strong> (Christie, Console): pause <code>reconcileLink</code>; on Cloud Run <code>ingestmemberupdate</code> → Permissions, remove <code>clayhub-link@</code>'s invoker (an emergency removal is allowed; granting by hand isn't, except Q9's recorded grant). Leave <code>recomputeStatuses</code> running — it only re-derives stored data. Trigger deliveries then get 403, throw, and Eventarc retries them for up to 24 h; the sender-non-2xx alert fires (at most one email per hour).</li>
248:  <li><strong>Then</strong> record it: a guarded release of <code>members</code> with <code>invoker: ["private"]</code> (sha phrase), attested (its schedule is still enabled, so the scheduler reading passes).</li>
249:  <li><strong>To resume</strong>: fix the cause; guarded release with the declared invoker; resume <code>reconcileLink</code>; Force run it to catch up whatever the 24-hour retry window dropped.</li>
250:  <li><strong>A stop email</strong> (409 or recompute stop): read the logged counts; if the change is real (e.g. many pauses start on the 1st), set <code>settings/linkLimits</code> with a higher limit and an <code>expiresAt</code> within 24 h, then Force run the job; otherwise stop the link and investigate.</li>
