/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:57:<tr><td>J1</td><td><code>functions:list</code> shows a scheduled v2 function only as <code>scheduleTrigger: {}</code> plus the label <code>deployment-scheduled: "true"</code> (<code>gcp/cloudfunctionsv2.js:299-305</code>; labels are copied through). Schedule, time zone, retry settings, deadline and target are not visible to the CLI.</td><td>The Scheduler job is read by Christie and checked by the script (V2). The guard can't prove the schedule; it proves her reading matches (V2).</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:59:<tr><td>J3</td><td>For a scheduled function the CLI <strong>forces</strong> the Cloud Run service-level <code>run.invoker</code> binding to exactly <code>[runtime account]</code>, on create and update (<code>release/fabricator.js:382-389, 484-492</code>).</td><td>The declaration has no invoker; the expected one is derived (V3).</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:61:<tr><td>J5</td><td>The job is only patched when schedule, time zone, deadline or retry changed; retry is compared with a <strong>partial</strong> match, so live retry fields not in the code are neither cleared nor noticed (<code>cloudscheduler.js:82-108</code>). The job is created/patched <strong>after</strong> the function (<code>fabricator.js:161, 182</code>): a failed job upsert leaves a live function with no (or an old) job and a non-zero exit. Removing a schedule from code orphans the job: it keeps POSTing.</td><td>V3 requires all five retry values; V2 reads the whole job; the runbook covers each partial state.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:62:<tr><td>J6</td><td>onSchedule pre-fills <code>timeZone</code> and all five retry keys with a reset marker that serialises to <code>null</code> (<code>runtime/manifest.js:32-45, 113-135</code>), so an unset field is <em>present</em> as <code>null</code>. <code>requiredAPIs</code> is a list of <code>{api, reason}</code> objects: <code>[{api: "cloudscheduler.googleapis.com", reason: …}]</code>. The handler's <code>event.scheduleTime</code> is the <code>X-CloudScheduler-ScheduleTime</code> header, or now if absent; a thrown error is logged with <code>logger.error</code> and answered 500; the wrapper writes the response itself (<code>v2/providers/scheduler.js:42-66</code>).</td><td>V3 checks numbers and the string <code>"UTC"</code>, not presence; O6.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:67:<tr><td>J11</td><td>Scheduler: <code>retryCount</code> 0–5 — retried that many times "or until the next scheduled execution, whichever first"; <code>maxRetryDuration</code> 0 = unlimited, and when both are set it retries until <em>both</em> limits are reached. A late response is cancelled as <code>DEADLINE_EXCEEDED</code>; whether the Cloud Run request keeps running is undocumented.</td><td>V6 (<code>maxRetrySeconds: 0</code>), V7 (own wait budget).</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:71:<tr><td>J15</td><td>Cloud Scheduler: the <code>X-CloudScheduler-ScheduleTime</code> header "contains the original scheduled invocation time and remains constant across retry attempts" (<a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/scheduler/docs/creating">Manage cron jobs</a>).</td><td>V7's key (the date of the scheduled time) is the same for a run and all its retries.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:72:<tr><td>J16</td><td><strong>Undocumented:</strong> when Google creates the Firestore service agent, and whether a PERMISSION_DENIED from an export names the principal. Documented: its address form, <code>service-&lt;PROJECT_NUMBER&gt;@gcp-sa-firestore.iam.gserviceaccount.com</code> (project number 760301318440), and that a bucket in another project needs an explicit grant.</td><td>V-4 step 7 has a written branch for each case.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:79:<tr><td>V2</td><td><strong>The Scheduler read-back is Christie's Console reading, checked by the script.</strong> <code>--attest</code> evidence gains two keys, <strong>always present</strong>, for every codebase: <code>schedulerJobList</code> (every job name in <code>us-central1</code>, a complete list, as the Console shows it) and <code>schedulerJobs</code> (one entry per scheduled function <em>of this codebase</em>: name, state, schedule, timeZone, targetUri, httpMethod, oidcServiceAccount, oidcAudience, body, headers, attemptDeadline and the five retry values). The script requires:
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:84:  <strong>Transcription format</strong> (like role ids): durations as whole seconds, numbers not text — <code>attemptDeadline: 1800</code>, <code>retryCount: 3</code>, <code>maxRetrySeconds: 0</code>, <code>minBackoffSeconds: 600</code>, <code>maxBackoffSeconds: 3600</code>, <code>maxDoublings: 2</code> — whatever the Console displays ("30m", "10m"); the template says so.<br>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:87:<tr><td>V3</td><td><strong>The guard's rules for a schedule</strong> (F13 amended for schedules only):
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:89:  <li>a declaration's <strong>key set is exact</strong>: HTTP <code>{trigger: "https", serviceAccount, invoker, ingress}</code>; schedule <code>{trigger: "schedule", serviceAccount, ingress, schedule: {schedule, timeZone, retryCount, maxRetrySeconds, minBackoffSeconds, maxBackoffSeconds, maxDoublings}}</code>. Any unknown or missing key refuses by name.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:91:  <li><code>scheduleTrigger</code>'s <code>schedule</code> and <code>timeZone</code> are strings and its five retry values are <strong>numbers</strong>, each equal to the declaration (J6: <code>null</code> means "unset" and refuses); <code>timeZone</code> must be <code>"UTC"</code>;</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:93:  <li>a schedule's expected <code>run.invoker</code> (for <code>--attest</code>) is exactly <code>serviceAccount:&lt;its runtime account&gt;</code> (J3); <code>timeoutSeconds</code> ≤ 1800; the other F14 rules unchanged.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:99:  <li>The Firestore service agent: <code>projects/tinker-hq-vault/roles/firestoreExportWriter</code> (the four J8 permissions) on the vault bucket only, granted in V-4 (bootstrap).</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:102:  Admin clients are built with explicit project and database names (no project discovery). <code>actAs</code> comes from Christie's Owner role (M7). Any widening needs the exact denied permission from a real error and Christie's approval.</td><td>Parent D-4. The two <code>tinker-hq-vault</code> grants can't be read by <code>--attest</code> (it reads only <code>my-clay-hub</code>'s IAM); V-1/V-4 screenshots plus V-4/V-5 behaviour are their record.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:104:<tr><td>V6</td><td><strong><code>vaultExport</code> limits:</strong> <code>retryCount: 3</code>, <code>maxRetrySeconds: 0</code>, <code>minBackoffSeconds: 600</code>, <code>maxBackoffSeconds: 3600</code>, <code>maxDoublings: 2</code> → retries about 10, 20 and 40 min after each failed attempt ends, then stop (J11; observed in V-4). A fast failure finishes the series in about 1¼ h; attempts that each run to the 1,500 s budget stretch it to about 2¾ h. <code>timeoutSeconds: 1800</code>, <code>maxInstances: 1</code>, <code>concurrency: 1</code>, <code>cpu: 1</code>, <code>memory: 512MiB</code>, <code>ingressSettings: ALLOW_ALL</code> (as the canary; Scheduler calls the public URL with a token).</td><td>A failed Sunday run gets three more tries the same morning. 512 MiB is cheap headroom for the gRPC admin client.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:108:  <li><strong>Running already?</strong> List this database's operations (<code>listOperationsAsync</code> on <code>projects/my-clay-hub/databases/(default)</code>, paged, filtered client-side to exports whose prefix starts <code>gs://&lt;bucket&gt;/weekly/D-</code>; <strong>cap: 1,000 operations examined</strong>, and hitting it throws — never "none"). A listed operation's <code>metadata</code> is a raw <code>google.protobuf.Any</code> (Firestore 9.3.0 <code>firestore_admin_v1_proto_api.d.ts:10355</code>): it is decoded with the pinned protobuf <strong>only</strong> when its type URL is exactly <code>type.googleapis.com/google.firestore.admin.v1.ExportDocumentsMetadata</code>, and the numeric <code>operationState</code> is mapped to its name. An operation with another type URL is not an export and is skipped; export metadata that fails to decode, or has an unknown state, throws (never treated as "not ours"). One not done → wait on it. One done <code>SUCCESSFUL</code> but no complete folder → throw (inconsistent: needs a person). Ones done <code>FAILED</code>/<code>CANCELLED</code> (or with <code>error</code>) are history: logged, never resumed, and their prefixes never reused → go to step 3. (This is V-4's bootstrap path.)</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:111:  Waiting polls every 15 s with a <strong>budget of 1,500 s from the start of the run</strong>; on expiry it throws ("still running; the retry resumes"), so the error path and alert always run before Cloud Run's 1,800 s kill. Success needs: <code>done</code>, no <code>error</code>, state <code>SUCCESSFUL</code>, the expected prefix, and the complete folder visible in the bucket. Anything else throws.<br>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:112:  <strong>Duplicates:</strong> two runs racing within seconds, or a lost reply that Google hasn't listed by the next retry, can each start an export. Each goes to its own prefix, so the result is two complete copies. At most one export per invocation, and at most 4 invocations per scheduled run. A Force run on another day gets its own key (an honest extra copy).<br>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:121:<tr><td>V14</td><td><strong>Restore runbook</strong> <code>docs/my-clay-hub/DATA-RESTORE.md</code>: choose the newest <strong>complete</strong> folder (its metadata file present and named after it — lifecycle deletes folders gradually, so a folder can be half there); the temporary read grant (<code>storage.buckets.get</code> + <code>storage.objects.get</code>) for the <em>importing</em> database's Firestore service agent, removed afterwards; an import <strong>overwrites matching documents and deletes nothing</strong>, so into a non-empty database it is a merge, not a rollback. The rehearsal happens in Phase E (O3).</td><td>Parent D-4.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:129:<tr><td>O3</td><td>Rehearse a restore now or after Phase E?</td><td>After Phase E (real data); added to Phase E's checklist in V-6.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:131:<tr><td>O5</td><td>Strict lock or allow a rare second copy?</td><td><strong>Allow a rare second copy</strong> (V7): each run writes to its own folder, so the worst case is two complete copies, never a mixed one. Changes the outline's "retries never make a second export" to "a retry never starts a second export when the first is visible".</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:136:<p>Order: <strong>V-0 → V-1 → V-2 → V-3 → V-4 → V-5 → V-6</strong>. V-0/V-1 (Console) and V-2 (guard code) can run in parallel. V-3 needs V-0's Monitoring agent address (for <code>vaultFresh</code>'s declared invoker) and V-1's bucket name, so it can't finish before them. V-2 and V-3 are each one branch and one PR, reviewed (Codex + Claude), then merged. Nothing is released before V-4.</p>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:148:  <li>Monitoring → Uptime checks → Create: choose "Service agent authentication"; read the Monitoring service agent's address shown; cancel. Record it verbatim. (This may provision the agent; that's expected and it must exist before V-4.)</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:159:Then nothing waits on it: V-4 step 7 finds the principal (the page, the log, or the documented fallback)
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:174:  <li>The new bucket → Permissions → grant <code>vaultLister</code> to <code>vault-export@my-clay-hub.iam.gserviceaccount.com</code> and <code>vault-watch@my-clay-hub.iam.gserviceaccount.com</code>. <strong>No grant to the Firestore agent yet</strong> (V-4's bootstrap; it doubles as the failure test). If domain-restricted sharing refuses a cross-project principal, stop and record the message.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:195:  <li><strong>Prove the shapes first</strong>, offline: a Node 22 unit test that requires the installed firebase-functions 7.4.0, calls <code>onSchedule({…V5/V6…}, …)</code>, and asserts <code>__endpoint.scheduleTrigger</code> and <code>__requiredAPIs</code> whole; and the same with one retry field omitted (→ <code>null</code>). No CLI, no <code>firebase.json</code>. Also prove the Functions emulator (<code>emulators:exec --only functions</code>) loads a codebase containing an <code>onSchedule</code> (a scratch fixture with its own <code>firebase.json</code>, as <code>env-probe</code> does).</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:199:  <li>The fake CLI synthesizes live scheduled entries (<code>scheduleTrigger: {}</code> + the label, camelCase job id). Refusal tests (each: refused by name, no deploy, no tag): a retry value <code>null</code>; a retry value ≠ declaration; <code>schedule</code> ≠ declaration; <code>timeZone</code> <code>null</code> or not <code>"UTC"</code>; timeout &gt; 1800; <code>requiredAPIs</code> extra entry, wrong shape, or present on an HTTP-only codebase; declared schedule but HTTP in code, and the reverse; an unknown declaration key (<code>"triger"</code>); invoker on a schedule declaration; a live scheduled function without the label, or an HTTP one with it; the probe answering a scheduled function. Attestation tests: wrong job name or case; state PAUSED; wrong OIDC account; an audience ≠ <code>uri</code>; a body or header; deadline ≠ 1800 s; each retry field off; target ≠ live <code>uri</code>; an extra or missing job in <code>schedulerJobList</code>; a missing key; a duration as text (<code>"30m"</code>); <code>core</code> whose list holds exactly <code>vault</code>'s declared job → <code>scheduler_attested=n/a</code>, and with an extra job → <code>no</code>, <code>iam_attested</code> unaffected either way; <strong>a regression test over a copy of the real <code>functions-core-attest/20261001T141405Z-7efa0f0</code> record</strong> → <code>--status --codebase core</code> succeeds and shows <code>unknown (recorded before D-4)</code>. Every existing test passes unchanged <strong>except these, deliberately updated</strong>: <code>tests/unit/firebase-config.test.js:42</code> (the exact declaration assertion, now with <code>trigger</code>); <code>tests/functions/manifest.test.js:107</code> (compares every declaration with <code>core</code>'s discovered functions — filtered by codebase, and the new declaration schema validated); <code>deploy-functions.test.sh:439</code> (a <code>scheduleTrigger</code> was refused as "not an HTTP function"; now refused only when undeclared), <code>:444</code> (any <code>requiredAPIs</code> refused; now only on a codebase without a schedule), <code>:340</code> (the reading template's six keys; now eight), and the template output itself. (V-3 updates the same two files again for <code>vault</code>'s declarations.)</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:200:  <li><code>FUNCTIONS-ROLLBACK.md</code>: scope "HTTP and scheduled"; a new § <em>scheduled functions</em>: Pause is the immediate, reversible stop (never delete); the partial states (function live with no job; job left on the old schedule; a schedule removed from code leaves an orphaned job — pause it, with Christie's OK); what to do if the Scheduler reading fails (pause first, then diagnose). <code>CLAUDE.md</code>: O6's exception. DECISIONS #62 (F13 amended for schedules; V2/V3; O6).</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:206:Then it refuses ("vault/vaultExport: retry maxDoublings is not a number (V3)") before any upload, and writes no tag
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:229:  <li><code>functions/vault/</code> per V1: <code>package.json</code> + lockfile, <code>reached.js</code>, <code>index.js</code> with <code>vaultExport</code> (<code>onSchedule</code>, every V5/V6 option written out) and <code>vaultFresh</code> (<code>onRequest</code>, every V9 option written out, <code>withReached</code>). The logic lives in two pure modules with injected clients: <code>export-run.js</code> (V7/V8) and <code>freshness.js</code> (V9). The bucket name and project are constants in one file (no params; F13).</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:233:    <li>V7: the per-run log line (scheduleTime, key, decision, prefix); a done-FAILED operation for today → a new prefix, never resumed; a complete folder → "already done", no export; a folder without its metadata file, or with a metadata name ≠ folder name, is not complete; a running operation → resumed, none started; "the export succeeded but the run died before returning" → no second export; a failed attempt → a new prefix; an operation for another date ignored; an operation not visible on the first retry but visible on the next; operation-list pagination, and the cap (1,000) → throws (never "none"); <strong>production-shaped encoded <code>Any</code> fixtures</strong> (built with the pinned protobuf): an export decoded correctly; an index-build operation skipped; a malformed export payload or unknown state → throws; <strong>Storage folder responses in the real client shape</strong> (<code>apiResponse.prefixes</code> across two pages via <code>nextQuery</code>; files-only responses never read as "no folders"); the 50-folder cap at 50 (ok) and 51 (throws); a <code>SUCCESSFUL</code> operation with no complete folder → throws; <code>done</code> with a missing or unknown state → throws; <code>error</code> set → throws; a wrong prefix → throws; transient list/get errors → throw (retry), never "start"; the wait budget → throws at 1,500 s; two concurrent runs → two distinct prefixes, never one shared; the key with the header missing and across a year end.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:241:<p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the code only reports success when Google says the export finished cleanly and the complete folder is in the bucket; a retry never starts a second export when the first is visible; a duplicate can only ever be a separate complete copy; the freshness endpoint answers "stale" after 7 days 18 hours. All proven without touching Google.</p>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:248:Then the run throws (logged as an error), and the next retry resumes waiting on the same operation
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:255:<!-- V-4 -->
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:257:<h3>V-4 — Deploy, read back, failure-first bootstrap, first export (the Phase E gate) <span class="status-tag ready">execution-ready: true</span></h3>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:265:  <li><strong>Failure first (bootstrap):</strong> Cloud Scheduler → the job → Force run. The Firestore agent has no grant on the bucket yet, so the export is expected to fail. Confirm: the function's log line shows <code>scheduleTime</code>, the key and the prefix, then an error; and the <strong>failure email arrives</strong> (note the delay). Note whether Scheduler retried, at what spacing, and that the retries logged the same <code>scheduleTime</code> (V6, J15).</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:267:  <li>Force run (after a few minutes for the grant to propagate): one new prefix <code>weekly/&lt;date&gt;-&lt;6&gt;</code>, "export complete", and the folder holds its <code>.overall_export_metadata</code>. If it's denied a storage permission instead, stop: record the exact permission; any widening (J8's Storage Admin fallback) needs Christie's OK and goes into V12's residual. <strong>While that export is still running</strong> (impl review round 1, Claude): Christie opens the new folder in the bucket. Its <code>.overall_export_metadata</code> file must <em>not</em> be there yet, only once the operation is done, because "complete folder" (J10) is what every success and the freshness check rely on. If it appears before the operation is done, stop: the completeness test is revised before V-4 continues.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:268:  <li><strong>Force run again, same day:</strong> the log says "already done"; no new folder, no new operation.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:270:  <li>Decisions log: receipt tags, folder, operation name, durations, the retry observation. OPEN-ITEMS.md and the foundation plan's Phase E gate: <strong>lifted</strong>, citing the three record fields and the folder.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:274:When the first Force run exports
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:281:Given the Scheduler reading shows a retry value different from the code
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:294:<p><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the freshness email was seen; the binding is back exactly; the first unattended Sunday export completed. <strong>Accepted:</strong> step 1 silences the freshness alarm for about 6 hours after V-4 lifted the Phase E gate; the export itself is unaffected. If real data has already loaded, run V-5 between Sunday exports.</p>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:312:  <li>Resilience report row <code>#app-my-clay-hub</code>: the vault bucket, the three accounts/agents and their roles in each project, the first export, both alerts; the two <code>tinker-hq-vault</code> grants' record (V-1/V-4 screenshots + behaviour); residual risk ("weekly off-project copy since &lt;date&gt;"; V12).</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:314:  <li>Phase E's checklist gains: after the first real member load, Force run and confirm the export completed; the restore rehearsal (O3).</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:325:<tr><td>Emulator-only tests?</td><td>Yes; the export logic is tested with fake clients and a surface check on the real ones. Real behaviour is proven in V-4/V-5.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:333:  <li><strong>V-0/V-1 halfway:</strong> visible in the Console; re-read and continue from the first step not done. Nothing uses the accounts or bucket until V-4.</li>
